  "name": "Stars and Stripes (America250)",
  "kind": "special",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "B78X",
  "description": "Fuselage: Forward fuselage bright royal blue nose to wing, belly included; aft fuselage a darker navy. Cheatlines: Red and white flag stripes divide the two: at the crown a red and a white band just behind the wing's trailing edge, curving down and forward to run along the belly under the wing as alternating red and white stripes. Tail: Standard United blue fin with the light-blue globe. Engines: Blue cowlings with polished lips. Winglets: none on the 787-10 (raked tips). Titles: Large, widely spaced white 'UNITED' capitals over the forward windows. Artwork: About 50 white stars spread over the navy aft fuselage behind the stripes.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://simpleflying.com/united-airlines-stunning-boeing-737-787-america-250-liveries/",
      "accessed": "2026-11-12"
