    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N91007.jpg",
      "title": "N91007 (CC BY-SA 4.0)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-12",
      "note": "Left side from below and ahead, 2026-08-12 (787-10 N91007): the two blues, the red and white stripes, the star field, titles, fin, engines. The only photo of the scheme found on Commons."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Drawn from one left-side photo of the 787-10 N91007 (2026-08-12); the right side and the 737-800 N78285 weren't seen in any openly licensed photo. The 737's version may place the stripes differently (shares are taken from the 787). The stripes under the wing are partly hidden by the flaps and gear; the lower red stripe there is low confidence. Small markings (Star Alliance badge by the forward door, a line of text under the cockpit, the reported tribute plaque) aren't drawn. One source misprinted the registration as N911007; FAA/Commons support N91007. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the navy field's edge and the stripes' sweep forward from the crown drawn as curves (corners at the stripes' square forward ends); title already measured. No new photo of either airframe was found; the 737-800 N78285's version is still unseen.",
  "from": "2026-06",
